 "final_summary": "The bug was that date-only due dates (e.g., '2026-09-09') were incorrectly parsed as midnight (00:00:00Z) instead of the end of the day (23:59:59Z). The fix in `tracker/timeutil.py` modifies `parse_datetime` to interpret bare date strings as the end of the day in UTC. This ensures the correct behavior as specified in the issue.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/timeutil.py b/tracker/timeutil.py\nindex 49fe1ca..3e66360 100644\n--- a/tracker/timeutil.py\n+++ b/tracker/timeutil.py\n@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ def parse_datetime(value, field=\"due_at\"):\n     try:\n         if len(text) == 10:\n             day = datetime.strptime(text, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n-            return datetime.combine(day, time(0, 0, 0), tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n+            return datetime.combine(day, time(23, 59, 59), tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n         parsed = datetime.fromisoformat(text)\n     except ValueError as exc:\n         raise ValidationError(f\"{field} is not a valid date\", {field: \"invalid\"}) from exc\n",
